  "reason": "Evidence: The strongest result so far is config_002 (RNA-only, multiprofile, PCA, avgpool) at 0.591 acc, a ~10.6% improvement over the singleprofile baseline (config_001, 0.485). This confirms multiprofile aggregation is highly beneficial. Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether a transformer-based aggregation would further improve over simple average pooling, or whether avgpool is already near-optimal for this setup. This experiment (config_003) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other factors constant (RNA-only, multiprofile, PCA n2000), giving a clean isolation of the aggregation strategy. It is the best next step because it directly extends the best-performing configuration with a single-variable change, reducing uncertainty about a key design decision before investing budget in more complex choices (new encoders, multimodal fusion, or better image backbones)."
}

